    "created_at": "2019-12-06T04:46:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-12-06T04:49:20Z",
    "body": "Argh, can we please please PLEASE not get into the habit of using single letter variable names for things (like `W`). It makes specs awful to read:\r\n\r\n> When the current high resolution time is greater than or equal to the last activation timestamp in W, W is said to have sticky activation.\r\n\r\nIt means we need to backtrack to figure out the type of `W`. HTML doesn't have type annotations, so this makes it somewhat annoying to find where is defined (specially as a spec grows).     ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
